This plugin includes protocol-helper code adapted from Marc Ford's
gmessages-omarchy-plugin (MIT):

  https://github.com/MarcFord/gmessages-omarchy-plugin

The Google Messages web protocol implementation is from the mautrix
project's libgm (go.mau.fi/mautrix-gmessages). That work remains theirs.
Its vendored LICENSE contains GNU AGPL version 3, with upstream exceptions
in LICENSE.exceptions. These notices are retained; OmaChat's root MIT
license does not relicense this dependency.

The Omarchy shell plugin (manifest, service lifecycle, and QML panel)
is OneLegDave's work.

The vendored libgm client includes a local synchronization patch: tachyon
token updates share the cookie lock used when saving the session. This keeps
token rotation from racing with JSON serialization. Preserve this patch when
updating the vendored dependency. Upstream authorship and license remain intact.

WhatsApp support vendors go.mau.fi/whatsmeow and related go.mau.fi modules
under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. Those files remain MPL-2.0; this plugin
does not relicense them. github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 is MIT and is linked
through CGO for the WhatsApp session database.

Telegram support vendors github.com/gotd/td and its transitive dependencies
under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, and BSD-3-Clause). Upstream
authorship and licenses remain intact.

